{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hrm1JLUzMtvHEpeFrFVXBm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage steps\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"fmt\"\n5\t\t\"io\"\n6\t\t\"net/http\"\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"regexp\"\n9\t\t\"strings\"\n10\t\t\"time\"\n11\t)\n12\t\n13\t// Word mapping (docs/architecture/architecture.yaml):\n14\t//   MCP server       - 127.0.0.1 at the port MCP_PORT names, 7411 when unset;\n15\t//                      answers GET /healthz with 200 once ready.\n16\t//   session          - opened by JSON-RPC 2.0 \"initialize\" POSTed to /mcp with\n17\t//                      Content-Type application/json; the reply is the opening.\n18\t//   ticket           - X-Session-Ticket of that reply: 32 lowercase hex chars.\n19\t//   protocol version - X-MCP-Protocol of that reply: a date in YYYY-MM-DD form.\n20\tconst (\n21\t\tdefaultMCPPort    = \"7411\"\n22\t\thealthDeadline    = 5 * time.Second\n23\t\thealthPollEvery   = 50 * time.Millisecond\n24\t\tinitializeRequest = `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"}`\n25\t)\n26\t\n27\tvar (\n28\t\t// A ticket is 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters, nothing else.\n29\t\tticketPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[0-9a-f]{32}$`)\n30\t\t// A protocol version is a date in YYYY-MM-DD form, such as 2025-06-18.\n31\t\tprotocolVersionPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`)\n32\t)\n33\t\n34\t// Register binds every phrase this suite's scenarios speak. One definition\n35\t// per catalogue phrase, anchored, with a capture group wherever the phrase\n36\t// varies, so a new scenario phrasing it the same way needs no new definition.\n37\tfunc Register(suite Suite) {\n38\t\tsuite.Step(`^the MCP server is running$`, givenTheMCPServerIsRunning)\n39\t\tsuite.Step(`^the (.+) opens a session$`, whenTheActorOpensASession)\n40\t\tsuite.Step(`^the session is granted a ticket$`, thenTheSessionIsGrantedATicket)\n41\t\tsuite.Step(`^the server names its protocol version$`, thenTheServerNamesI